libjpeg-turbo 2.0.4 WebAssembly JPEG decoder
--------------------------------------------

Upstream source: https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/tree/2.0.4
WebAssembly build source: https://github.com/LinusU/cwasm-jpeg-turbo
Pinned build commit: 61bcc6c3fa933c796ee9b64c5ea9821966ef8e42
Source package: @cwasm/jpeg-turbo 0.1.3
Package integrity: sha512-FkZxwwC6r4zhzlqM0nYGaMj/MDSrZPxLOdPdM6ySlgsMfOpNAZcLQkpNF4jP+DmsuUvRoeUD0YSMBvg3jYfK6w==
Package tarball SHA-256: 0ab9fcd1134d1190d8188d1a4110843613b563864f26cd740f91092be5807c0b
Shipped WASM byte length: 139151
Shipped WASM SHA-256: 80ed55eef2d0ff276f837ef521fad8181ccdfa6f298f652f6e45aed7fbbbc871

The pinned build uses Ubuntu 18.04, WASI SDK 10.0, Binaryen 1.39.1, disables
SIMD, and exports only memory allocation plus the TurboJPEG in-memory
decompression entry points used by HEPR. HEPR ships the resulting WASM binary,
not the @cwasm JavaScript wrapper or any of its runtime dependencies. The build
package declares the build integration as MIT licensed. Its notice is retained
below even though HEPR does not ship the package's JavaScript wrapper.

The libjpeg-turbo 2.0.4 license also identifies a zlib-licensed SIMD extension.
That code is not present in this artifact: the pinned Docker build passes
`-DWITH_SIMD=0`, compiles `jsimd_none.c`, and includes no source below the
upstream `simd/` directory.

